This pull request includes the follow changes:

- Compute Shader
- Resource Binding through shader variable instead of classic enum way
- Refactor View and ReflectionRender to this new way

This PR changes the old way of Compute Shader Dispatch made by rbfx, above you can see an example on how you must use the compute device.

Shader:
```
layout(binding = 0)
uniform sampler2D srcTex;
layout(binding = 1, rgba8)
uniform image2D outputTexture;

layout(local_size_x = 16, local_size_y = 16, local_size_z = 1) in;
void main() {
    //... Compute code
}
```
CPP Code:
```
Graphics* graphics = GetSubsystem<Graphics>();
ComputeDevice* computeDevice = GetSubsystem<ComputeDevice>();

computeDevice->SetReadTexture("srcTex", READ_RESOURCE);
computeDevice->SetWriteTexture("outputTexture", WRITE_RESOURCE);
computeDevice->SetProgram(graphics->GetShader(CS, "SHADER_PATH"));
computeDevice->Dispatch(X_DIM, Y_DIM, Z_DIM);
```

This PR contains 2 commits which should make the generated .class files more deterministic.

Essentially the problem is `Class#getDeclaredMethods` returns an undefined order, so even when a simple patch is applied to a stable version one ends up with a ton of .class files (mostly the "INVOKER" ones) *modified* in the resulting artifact (jruby-base.jar).

